PiBridge (VR hub for Pimax headsets on Linux; not affiliated with Pimax) contains code ported from omarchyvr
(https://github.com/laughtt/omarchyvr, by laughtt / José Mauricio Carpio Herrera and contributors), licensed MIT OR
Apache-2.0; it is used here under its MIT terms, reproduced below. The device descriptions in devices/ are copied
from omarchyvr unchanged. Files ported from omarchyvr say so in their second line.

Other third-party material in this tree:
- app/third_party/openvr/openvr.h: the OpenVR SDK header (Valve, BSD-3-Clause, see app/third_party/openvr/LICENSE).
  The app loads SteamVR's own libopenvr_api.so at run time; it is not part of this tree.
- tools/slam/data/basalt-euroc_config.json: Basalt's generic EuRoC VIO config (data/euroc/euroc_config.json of
  Basalt commit df6e970, https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mateosss/basalt, Copyright (c) 2019, Vladyslav Usenko and
  Nikolaus Demmel, BSD-3-Clause), unmodified, embedded into pibridge-slam as omarchyvr-slam embeds it.
- devices/dream-air/reference/ (headset-calibration.xml, lens.conf, gyro-bias): omarchyvr's Dream Air reference
  data (MIT, as above), every serial scrubbed there.
- app/src/qv/: settings and preview code from artscout-qv-vulkan-linux (MIT); each file says where it came from.
- patches/chovr/*.patch: changes to CustomHeadsetOpenVR (https://github.com/sboys3/CustomHeadsetOpenVR, sboys3),
  GPL-2.0 as CustomHeadsetOpenVR itself. They are not built into PiBridge.
- patches/nvidia/**/*.patch: changes to NVIDIA's open-gpu-kernel-modules, under that project's MIT/GPL-2.0 dual
  licence. The pre-Blackwell 2Heads1OR patches are omarchyvr's (one of them, the bounded EVO wait, by Rouan (rvdende),
  NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules PR #1262). Not built into PiBridge.
- patches/ (the rest): scripts, notes and rules from omarchyvr (MIT, as above). See patches/README.md.
- libpibridge-room/ and tools/roomsetup/: the room setup, ported in large part from ZoneTweak
  (https://github.com/killdano/ZoneTweak, Go, by killdano), MIT; its licence is reproduced at the end of this file.
  Each ported file says which ZoneTweak file it comes from.

- third_party/monado/: PiBridge's fork of Monado (https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/monado/monado, Collabora, Ltd. and
  the Monado contributors), BSL-1.0 (third_party/monado/LICENSES/BSL-1.0.txt; other files there carry their own SPDX
  lines). It includes the Pimax driver of omarchyvr's Monado fork (MIT OR Apache-2.0, as above) and PiBridge's changes
  (docs/monado.md). It reports itself as "Monado PiBridge fork from OmarchyVR"; Monado's copyright notices are kept in
  every file. It is built separately and is not linked into the PiBridge app.
- quadviews/: the quad views OpenXR layer, formerly the separate linux-vulkan-quadviews-openxr-layer (MIT,
  quadviews/LICENSE); its design follows mbucchia's Quad-Views-Foveated (no code taken).
- world/: PiBridge World, a Godot 4 project (our code, MIT). Godot itself (MIT, https://godotengine.org) is not part of
  this tree; the user downloads it.

Pimax, Crystal Super and Dream Air are trademarks of their owners. PiBridge is an independent project and is not made,
endorsed or supported by Pimax.

